Functional Requirements:
- Sampling and Storage: The circuit must be capable of receiving and maintaining a window containing exactly 4 of the most recent data samples.
- Average Calculation: The system must accumulate the values of these 4 samples (running sum) and divide by 4 to produce the average.
- Data Flow Control: The circuit is only allowed to update the window at each cycle if the input sample is confirmed to be valid.
- Status Reporting: The system must be able to recognize when its output data is reliable (after collecting the initial 4 samples) and assert a valid flag to notify the upper layer.

Resource Constraints: The design must be optimized to operate within a reference scale of approximately 200–280 standard cells.
